    {
      "id": "dbe9e290c19e47a1939c805977bad4a7",
      "title": "Kentucky Groundwater Karst Basins",
      "url": "https://kgs.uky.edu/arcgis/rest/services/KYWater/KYGWKarstBasins/MapServer",
      "publisher": "Kentucky_DGI",
      "status": "needs_review",
      "publisher_verified": false,
      "native_geography": null,
      "production_admission": false,
      "properties": {
        "snippet": "Geographical locations of karst groundwater basins, groundwater flowpaths, and dye injection/recovery points in Kentucky",
        "extent": null,
        "commentsEnabled": true,
        "groupDesignations": null,
        "access": "public",
        "apiToken2ExpirationDate": -1,
        "typeKeywords": [
          "ArcGIS Server",
          "Data",
          "Map Service",
          "Service",
          "Metadata"
        ],
        "description": "Geographical locations of karst groundwater basins, groundwater \nflowpaths, and dye injection/recovery points in Kentucky. Dye tracing is\n a common method used for understanding groundwater movement. Dye is \npoured (or injected) into a sinking stream, well, sinkhole, or body of \nwater, where it is carried down-gradient by flowing water. The locations\n at which dye is recovered (typically at artesian springs) indicates a \nconnection from injection to recovery site. This connection is refered \nto as a groundwater flowpath. Conducting multiple dye traces across an \narea allows for the interpretation of regional groundwater flow by \nassessing where flowpaths either converge or remain distinct. \nGroundwater basin boundaries can then be delineated, however unlike \nsurficial watersheds, karst groundwater basins may differ significantly \ndue to variations in subsurface hydrogeologic configurations and conduit\n geometries. During periods of increased flow, flowpaths may shift or \nhybridize with other flowpaths, creating overlapping basins. This \ndataset can be used for understanding the general flow of karst \ngroundwater but does not guarantee the absolute accuracy of groundwater \nflow or basin boundaries.",
        "licenseInfo": "LIMITATION OF LIABILITY: The Kentucky Division of Geographic Information  (DGI) has no indication or reason to believe that there are any  inaccuracies or defects of information incorporated in this work and  make no representations of any kind, including, but not limited to, the  warranties of merchantability or fitness for a particular use, nor are  any such warranties to be implied, with respect to the information or  data, furnished herein",
        "ownerId": "93a18f5539c1d9e5e337edceefb04652",
